-- title:
--   Theorem 1.5 — Pauli relative distance $d_{\mathrm{rel}}=d_{A\to B}\ge d_B$, strictness criterion and monotonicity
-- statement:
--   Let $a_i=\eta_i^AP_{n_A}(w_i)$ and $b_i=\eta_i^BP_{n_B}(v_i)$, $i=1,\dots,s$, be signed Pauli generators ($\eta_i^L\in\{\pm1\}$, $P_n(x,z)=i^{x\cdot z}X^xZ^z$), let $\mathcal A=C^*(I,a_1,\dots,a_s)$, and let $\pi$ be a unital $*$-homomorphism on $\mathcal A$ with $\pi(a_i)=b_i$. Let $K_A=\ker[w_1\cdots w_s]$ and $K_B=\ker[v_1\cdots v_s]$ over $\mathbb F_2$, $|c|$ the Hamming weight, $d_{A\to B}=\min\{|c|:c\in K_B\setminus K_A\}$, $d_B=\min\{|c|:0\ne c\in K_B\}$ (empty minima $+\infty$), and $d_{\mathrm{rel}}$ the intrinsic relative distance of $\pi$ (Definition 4.1). Then
--
--   1. $d_{\mathrm{rel}}=d_{A\to B}$;
--   2. $d_{A\to B}\ge d_B$;
--   3. $K_A=\{0\}\implies d_{A\to B}=d_B$;
--   4. if $d_B<\infty$, then
--   $$d_{A\to B}>d_B\iff\{c\in K_B:\ |c|=d_B\}\subseteq K_A;$$
--   5. for every subspace $K'$ with $K_A\subseteq K'\subseteq K_B$ (in particular the kernel $K_{A'}$ of any compatible source $A'$), $d_{A\to B}\le d_{A'\to B}:=\min\{|c|:c\in K_B\setminus K'\}$.
--
--   The theorem says that relative decoding absorbs the relations already present in the source: its distance is at least the ordinary distance of the target relation code, and strictly larger exactly when every shortest target relation is inherited. This is what can enlarge the transduction window $2D<d_{\mathrm{rel}}$ beyond the ordinary-decoding window $2D<d_B$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: (21) for compatible source choices A′ with kernels K_A ⊆ K_{A′} ⊆ K_B → clause 5 for every subspace K′ with K_A ≤ K′ ≤ K_B; reason: the kernel of every compatible source is such a subspace, so the Lean clause specializes to (21); App. B.1 shows every such K′ is realized
--   - encoding: aᵢ = ηᵢᴬ P_{n_A}(wᵢ), P_n(x, z) = i^{x·z}X^xZ^z with integer exponent x·z, ηᵢᴸ ∈ {±1}, wᵢ ∈ F₂^{2n_A} → pauliGen ηA wA i = ((ηA i : ℤ) : ℂ) • StabTestMem.weyl (wA i) on Qubits n = Fin n → Bool, ηA i ∈ ℤˣ, labels CutRankSched.Pauli n = (Fin n → ZMod 2) × (Fin n → ZMod 2); the label matrix has rows x then z (Fin n ⊕ Fin n); reason: the published StabTestMem.weyl is the Hermitian Pauli i^{x·z}X^xZ^z with the integer exponent; ℤˣ = {±1}; same operators and labels
--   - encoding: A = C∗(I_A, a₁,…,a_s) ⊆ B(H_A), π : A ↠ B unital ∗-homomorphism with π(aᵢ) = bᵢ → A = genAlg a = StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range a) in Matrix nA nA ℂ; π : genAlg a →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix nB nB ℂ with π (gen a i) = b i; reason: in finite dimension the generated ∗-subalgebra is norm closed (App. E, p.85); the range of π is the ∗-subalgebra generated by the bᵢ, i.e. B; this is the setting of the published relDist
--   - encoding: distances in ℕ₀ ∪ {+∞}, empty minimum +∞ → values in ℕ∞ defined by sInf, sInf ∅ = ⊤; reason: Lean convention; same values
-- source:
--   Shang, Stilck França, From Simple Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial Transduction via Relative Decoding, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…), Theorem 1.5, p.9 (pdf_page 9); body version Proposition 4.8, p.25; setting §4.4.1, eqs. (75)–(88), (93), pp.23–24

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LIDT_MIPStarRE_Quantum_FiniteMatrix_NormalizedTrace
