set_option autoImplicit false

namespace RelDecoding.Supplement

open QAlgorithms RelDecoding

/-- **Theorem 1.5 (Relative decoding has higher distance).** For signed Pauli generators
`aᵢ = ηᵢᴬ P_{n_A}(wᵢ)`, `bᵢ = ηᵢᴮ P_{n_B}(vᵢ)` and a unital ∗-homomorphism `π : A → B` with
`π(aᵢ) = bᵢ`, write `K_A = ker A`, `K_B = ker B` over `F₂`, `d_{A→B} = min{|c| : c ∈ K_B \ K_A}` and
`d_B = min{|c| : 0 ≠ c ∈ K_B}`. Then
1. `d_rel = d_{A→B}` (19);
2. `d_{A→B} ≥ d_B` (19);
3. `K_A = {0} ⟹ d_{A→B} = d_B` (19);
4. if `d_B < ∞`, then `d_{A→B} > d_B ⟺ {c ∈ K_B : |c| = d_B} ⊆ K_A` (20);
5. for kernels `K_A ⊆ K_{A′} ⊆ K_B`, `d_{A→B} ≤ d_{A′→B}` (21).

Shang, Stilck França, *From Simple Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial
Transduction via Relative Decoding*, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…),
Theorem 1.5, p.9 (body version Proposition 4.8, p.25; setting §4.4.1, pp.23–24).

**Formalization Note.** `P_n` is the published `StabTestMem.weyl` (Hermitian convention
`i^{x·z}X^xZ^z`, integer exponent) on `Qubits n = Fin n → Bool`; `A = genAlg a`; `π` maps into
`Matrix (Qubits n_B) (Qubits n_B) ℂ` with `π (gen a i) = b i` (its range is `B`), the setting of the
published `relDist`. All distances lie in `ℕ∞` with empty minimum `⊤`. Clause 5 is stated for every
subspace `K′` with `K_A ⊆ K′ ⊆ K_B` (App. B.1 realizes each as the kernel of a compatible source). -/
theorem theorem_1_5 {nA nB s : ℕ} (wA : Fin s → CutRankSched.Pauli nA) (ηA : Fin s → ℤˣ)
    (wB : Fin s → CutRankSched.Pauli nB) (ηB : Fin s → ℤˣ)
    (π : genAlg (pauliGen ηA wA) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Qubits nB) (Qubits nB) ℂ)
    (hπ : ∀ i, π (gen (pauliGen ηA wA) i) = pauliGen ηB wB i) :
    relDist (pauliGen ηA wA) π = coordDist (pauliKer wA) (pauliKer wB) ∧
      ordDist (pauliKer wB) ≤ coordDist (pauliKer wA) (pauliKer wB) ∧
      (pauliKer wA = ⊥ → coordDist (pauliKer wA) (pauliKer wB) = ordDist (pauliKer wB)) ∧
      (ordDist (pauliKer wB) < ⊤ →
        (ordDist (pauliKer wB) < coordDist (pauliKer wA) (pauliKer wB) ↔
          {c | c ∈ pauliKer wB ∧ (hammingNorm c : ℕ∞) = ordDist (pauliKer wB)} ⊆
            (pauliKer wA : Set (Fin s → ZMod 2)))) ∧
      (∀ K' : Submodule (ZMod 2) (Fin s → ZMod 2), pauliKer wA ≤ K' → K' ≤ pauliKer wB →
        coordDist (pauliKer wA) (pauliKer wB) ≤ coordDist K' (pauliKer wB)) := by sorry

end RelDecoding.Supplement
